course: dictionary
lesson: 8559
title: Scar: a mark that stays
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scar is a mark left on your skin after a cut, burn or wound has healed. Your body mends the damage, but the mend can leave a mark that stays.
explain: Context helps you. «A deep wound mends with tough fibres instead of ordinary skin, so it leaves a scar» tells you that a scar is different skin, left behind when a deep wound heals. A bruise is not a scar: «a knock that breaks tiny blood vessels without breaking the skin leaves a bruise» that changes colour as the body cleans it up.
explain: Scar can also be a verb: to scar means to leave a scar. «Scarred for life» means something bad has left a lasting mark, in feelings as well as on skin.
fact: A scar is a mark left on your skin after a cut, burn or wound has healed.
fact: «Scar» can also mean a lasting sign of a bad experience, in feelings or on land.
fact: «Scar» is also a verb: to scar means to leave a scar.
fact: In stories a scar can tell part of a character's past, like Harry Potter's lightning scar.
fact: An axolotl can regrow a lost leg without leaving a scar, so it is studied to help people heal better.
exercise: «Scratching chickenpox spots can cause infection and scars, so keep nails short.» What is a scar? | *A mark left on the skin after a wound has healed | A cooling lotion an adult gives you | A sweet treat from the shop | A loud noise
exercise: «A deep wound mends with tough fibres instead of ordinary skin, so it leaves a scar.» What does this tell you about a deep wound? | It leaves a bruise that changes colour | *It can leave a scar | It never heals at all | It is painless
exercise: «Keepers tell animals apart by marks, scars, shape and behaviour.» Which word means a mark left after a wound has healed? | *scars | behaviour | marks | shape
test: A story says, «Harry Potter's lightning scar.» What can a scar in a story tell us? | *Part of a character's past | How to bake a cake | The weather tomorrow | The time of day
test: To scar means what? | *To leave a scar | To wash a cut | To hide a mark | To stop a bruise from changing colour
exam: The axolotl regrows a lost leg «without leaving a scar», so what does that mean? | It loses the leg for good | It grows a scar on the leg | It shows a bad experience | *It heals with no mark left behind
